# MN Micro ERP - CODEOWNERS (example; replace @mn-erp/* with the real GitHub teams)
# Spec: docs/features/mn-micro-erp/18-dev-setup.md section 8.3.
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so generic rules come first and specific rules last.
# The main-branch ruleset requires "Review from Code Owners"; .github/workflows/sensitive-review.yml
# additionally requires 2 approvals for the posting / tax / numbering / eBarimt / migration paths.
# When a line lists several teams, an approval from ANY ONE of them satisfies the code-owner rule.
# Paths whose specific team MUST approve (tax, eBarimt, accountant sign-off) therefore list that team alone.
#
# Teams:
#   @mn-erp/tech-leads           architecture, build, anything not owned below
#   @mn-erp/ledger-owners        posting engine, G/L, sub-ledger application, numbering, money type
#   @mn-erp/tax-owners           VAT, city tax, tax parameters, tax reports
#   @mn-erp/ebarimt-owners       PosAPI adapter, outbox handlers for eBarimt
#   @mn-erp/accounting-reviewers accountants who sign golden scenarios (domain review, not code)
#   @mn-erp/platform             tenancy, identity, audit, integration/outbox, jobs
#   @mn-erp/frontend             web/
#   @mn-erp/devops               CI/CD, containers, deploy, database roles

# ---- Default ----
*                                               @mn-erp/tech-leads

# ---- Build, CI/CD, infrastructure ----
/.github/                                       @mn-erp/devops @mn-erp/tech-leads
/deploy/                                        @mn-erp/devops
/db/init/                                       @mn-erp/devops
/Directory.Build.props                          @mn-erp/tech-leads
/Directory.Packages.props                       @mn-erp/tech-leads
/BannedSymbols*.txt                             @mn-erp/tech-leads @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/global.json                                    @mn-erp/tech-leads
/nuget.config                                   @mn-erp/devops @mn-erp/tech-leads
/tools/licenses/                                @mn-erp/tech-leads

# ---- Frontend ----
/web/                                           @mn-erp/frontend
/tests/E2E/                                     @mn-erp/frontend

# ---- Platform ----
/src/Modules/Platform/                          @mn-erp/platform
/src/Modules/Integration/                       @mn-erp/platform
/src/Erp.Worker/                                @mn-erp/platform
/src/BuildingBlocks/                            @mn-erp/tech-leads

# ---- Ledger-critical code (posting, money, numbering) ----
/src/Modules/GeneralLedger/                     @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/src/Modules/Platform/*/Numbering/              @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/src/BuildingBlocks/Erp.BuildingBlocks.Domain/Monetary/  @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/tools/Erp.Analyzers/                           @mn-erp/ledger-owners @mn-erp/tech-leads
# Posting code of every module (any depth), FX revaluation.
/src/Modules/**/Posting/                        @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/src/Modules/**/Revaluation/                    @mn-erp/ledger-owners

# ---- Tax ----
/src/Modules/Tax/                               @mn-erp/tax-owners

# ---- eBarimt ----
/src/Modules/EBarimt/                           @mn-erp/ebarimt-owners
/deploy/posapi-mock/                            @mn-erp/ebarimt-owners

# ---- Database migrations: one approval from ledger owners OR devops satisfies the code-owner rule;
#      sensitive-review.yml requires a second approval. Request both teams on every schema change. ----
/db/migrations/                                 @mn-erp/ledger-owners @mn-erp/devops
/src/Erp.Migrator/                              @mn-erp/devops @mn-erp/ledger-owners

# ---- Tests that encode accounting truth ----
/tests/Golden/                                  @mn-erp/ledger-owners
/tests/Golden/Scenarios/                        @mn-erp/accounting-reviewers
/tests/Architecture/                            @mn-erp/tech-leads
